version: 1.18.1

## How changelog entries are written

This changelog is read by the dashboard (click the version badge) and is written
for the person running AMMO campaigns — not for AMMO's maintainers. Every entry
answers one question: what changed for me? A new capability, something that got
faster or more reliable, a bug I might have hit, or a dependency / model / GPU
change that affects what my sessions run on.

Two tiers per entry:

- Highlights — top-level "- " bullets. Plain language, user impact first. These
  are the only lines the dashboard shows.
- Details — indented ("  - ") sub-bullets beneath a highlight. File paths, test
  counts, schema internals, and other engineering specifics live here for
  maintainers. The dashboard parser skips indented lines, so details never
  appear in the UI.

Start each highlight with one tag. Use plain text — the UI shows tags literally,
so do NOT use markdown (no "**Fix**"):

- New — a capability you can now use.
- Improved — existing behavior is faster, more accurate, or more reliable.
- Fixed — something that was broken now works.
- Changed — a default or behavior changed that you should know about. For a
  breaking change, lead with Changed and state the migration.
- Updated — a dependency, model, or GPU bump that affects what sessions run on.

Drop anything a campaign operator would never notice (pure refactors, doc edits,
test-only changes, internal renames) from the highlights — demote it to a detail
line or leave it out. If a release is entirely internal, write one honest
highlight describing the net effect (e.g. "more consistent across models").

When you cut a release, add its block at the top of "## Changelog" below, newest
first, and bump the "version:" line at the top of this file. Use a real date.
Example shape — the version header is indented here ONLY so this example is not
parsed as a real changelog entry; real entries start at column 0:

    ### 1.13.0 (2026-06-15)
    - New — One-line description of the capability.
      - Engineering detail for maintainers (not shown in the UI).

## Changelog

### 1.18.1 (2026-08-12)
- Updated — Debate and implementation champions now run Claude Opus 5 (was Claude Fable 5), so the default configuration works with any Anthropic API key. Every model pin is documented and user-changeable; see docs/AMMO_DEEP_DIVE.md "Which Model Runs Which Agent".
  - `agents/ammo-champion.md` and `agents/ammo-impl-champion.md` model → `opus`; `models.json` roster updated in the same edit; `fable` alias removed.

### 1.18.0 (2026-07-29)
- New — Mining tables are now generated, not hand-written: `scripts/mine_trace.py` computes every number in the Workload Dilution and Top Components tables directly from the nsys sqlite traces and emits `rounds/{N}/mining/mined.json` + `tables.md`. The researcher authors the config (segmentation policy, family labels) and writes prose around the generated tables. This removes the transcription-drift class that cost one campaign six audit cycles.
  - Interval-union busy (never sums concurrent kernels), wall-denominated decode share derived from `decode_avg_s / avg_s` (never a stored field), exhaustive symbol→family partition with residual disclosure, step-count fallback ladder with recorded source, FATAL on out-of-bounds decode_busy or non-exhaustive partition. Reproduces the published qwen3.5-4B round-1 tables exactly. `ammo_state.py` enrichment reads mined.json first (markdown parse is the fallback); audit-invariants' phase-accounting duties collapse from recompute-the-arithmetic to verify-the-inputs.
- New — `scripts/preflight_vllm_api.py` checks every vLLM symbol the sweep couples to (GPU-free, import+introspection) so a vLLM upgrade fails loudly at campaign start instead of silently degrading measurements mid-round. The sweep also stamps `vllm_version` into results, warns on cross-version baseline imports, refuses cross-method throughput comparisons, and derives the nsys trace preset from target.json hardware.
- Changed — Both variants now render from one canonical source: `ai_cli_session/_ammo_shared/` (61 files) + `scripts/render_ammo_variants.py`, with a sha256 parity test. Twin drift is now a test failure, not a silent divergence.
  - gpu_reservation superset upstreamed (child-reservation reaping — fixes a Claude-variant GPU leak on dead subagents); one shared state.schema.json (optional `codex_thread_id`); inert model frontmatter stripped from codex agent files.
- Fixed — Blocking hooks that could be bypassed now actually block: an inspection prefix no longer disables the pretool guard's hard blocks (per-segment classification via shared `hook_cmd_classify.py`), path-qualified/nested pip installs are caught, subagents can no longer rewrite `skills/ammo/scripts/` or `schemas/` (the Mechanical Authorities), the audit-phase2 Stop guard fires (marker-name mismatch fixed), and `reconcile_track_state.py --write` goes through state validation.
  - `_ammo_is_lead.sh` L4 fail-open inverted; env-default-guard broadened to any truthy-default `VLLM_*` gating flag with an explicit infra allowlist; every fix landed with a red→green bypass harness case.
- Fixed — Compaction checkpoints survive real summaries: precompact/postcompact build JSON via jq instead of shell interpolation (a multi-line or quoted round summary no longer corrupts the checkpoint). Hook timeouts corrected to seconds.
- New — One machine-readable `scripts/artifact_layout.json` (45 slots) now feeds both variants' layout-warn hooks; the 4 known false-warn paths (evidence.json, validation_summary.json, diff.patch, post_ship_profiling) are fixed and a parity test pins manifest↔doc agreement.
- New — `ammo_state.py ingest-baseline` reads the sweep's e2e_latency_results.json straight into state.json through the validated write path, removing the last hand-retyped numbers on the Stage-1 critical path. Gate enrichment walks the schema contract names; per-BS gate reconciliation replaces the single-row guard; debate EV-identity and tier-cap checks run mechanically.
- Changed — `collect_env.py` deleted (produced zero env.json across 209 archived campaigns); docs no longer assert the removed tmux deny rule; codex session downloads now strip `.codex/` and `AGENTS.md` (sanitization gap); Dockerfile template-copy depth fixed; `models.json` is the single model roster with an agreement test; the internal intent map gained a `file` field on all 162 entries and a bidirectional closure test so it cannot silently rot.

