### 1.14.0 (2026-07-10)
- New — A kernel win that is real but too diluted to move end-to-end latency can now ship through a dedicated DILUTED_PASS path instead of being discarded: the track passes if its decode-phase improvement is statistically significant and comfortably above noise, prefill is not significantly regressed at any batch size, end-to-end never drops below 1.0x, and the numbers are internally consistent. Diluted ships are marked as such everywhere they appear.
  - Sweep now emits per-iteration `prefill_iter_means_s` / `decode_iter_means_s` plus row-level `phase_significance` (Welch, omit-not-null); report adds `e2e_gate.diluted_pass` with the 5 ship conditions (incl. Amdahl-consistency) and overrides the verdict to PASS. No new status enum: track stays PASS + `diluted: true` marker + round-level `diluted_tracks`. Accounting firewall: measured e2e (~1.00x) enters cumulative speedup, never TPOT; EV ranking stays on projected e2e. New BLOCKING S45 audit row 15 forces the marker; `score_campaign.py` keeps the base-score gate undiscounted but discounts diluted ships in the diversity bonus. 6 golden fixtures + 3 new test files; adversarially reviewed (4 HIGH findings fixed pre-merge).
- Changed — Design debates run leaner: in round 1 the proposal itself is the argument of record (the separate argument phase is gone), champions hand critiques to each other directly through a per-candidate ring instead of waiting on lead broadcasts each phase, and eligibility gate verdicts are recorded once at the Phase-0 gate and trusted by scoring instead of re-derived.
  - CUT-1..4 from the round-time redundancy audit. `ring_assignment` is emitted per minted op_id with a `target_section` field, so a champion owning multiple candidates gets full critique coverage without resolving anything itself. Done-signals are atomic write-temp+rename files; lead barriers kept only at the Phase-0 gate and the end-of-round open-items tally; lead liveness via artifact-dir polling with per-phase timeouts. Verdicts live in lead-owned `rounds/{CR}/debate/eligibility_verdicts.md` (hook-allowlisted); scoring re-derives only on elimination-capable Phase B/C evidence.
- Changed — Debate candidates are now ranked by expected value — P(success) x projected end-to-end gain, uncapped — with the old gates and caps acting as an eligibility filter, and the claim phase is replaced by portfolio selection: every champion analyzes the full profile and submits 2-3 ranked candidates, with diversity enforced at winner selection. Winner choices near the old thresholds may differ from earlier campaigns.
  - EV_pct elimination floor = `min_e2e_improvement_pct`; optional spawn-time lens hints replace component partitioning; cross-component proposals are first-class; the portfolio concentration rule guards diversity at Winner Selection.
- Changed — The ship gate now decides from a single launch's statistics: PASS requires the measured speedup to clear the configured floor and the improvement to be Welch-significant across per-iteration latencies. The multi-launch `--num-launches` approach is retired.
  - Floor = 1 + max(`min_e2e_improvement_pct`, `noise_tolerance_pct`)/100; gate-slot misinvocation guard; FP8 placeholder removed; new tolerance audit row; dead Pre-SHIP jq checks fixed.
- Improved — Background monitoring and audits cost less without watching less: the transcript monitor polls on a two-cadence model (~10s cheap collision/liveness tick, ~45s full transcript analysis, 5s floor when suspicious) and no longer sends routine interim pings; audits do simple arithmetic checks inline instead of spawning a delegate for each, and per-track Stage 4-5 evidence can be gathered early while other tracks are still validating.
  - CUT-6/7/8/9. The monitor's advisory checklist is deliberately unchanged — breadth kept over cost. Audit Lane A (inline, INVESTIGATOR-DIRECT citations) vs Lane B (delegate fan-out; Holistic row 1 stays Lane B permanently); early partials at `rounds/{N}/audits/stage_45_partial_{op_id}.md`, all deleted on any re-audit. Terminal DA-MONITOR SUMMARY remains unconditional.
- Fixed — Campaigns with legacy rounds no longer deadlock on every state write (the mining-enrichment non-null rule moved from a schema constraint to a round-advance gate), and an exhausted audit loop now quarantines and re-audits only the affected tracks — the whole campaign pauses only for campaign-scoped findings.
  - +6 hook tests (ME1-ME6), +5 engine tests pin both legs. Also removed stale reference docs (code-templates.md, gpu-configs.md, optimization-techniques.md) and pinned the debate champion to the `fable` model alias (matching the impl champion).

### 1.13.0 (2026-07-08)
- Changed — A campaign now stops a state.json write when validation cannot run (for example a corrupted state.json, or a session environment missing the jsonschema library), instead of silently letting the bad write through. If you are in a deliberately degraded environment, set AMMO_VALIDATE_FAIL_OPEN=1 to restore the old permissive behavior.
  - Fail-closed is enforced via the PostToolUse decision:block payload from `ammo-state-validate.sh` / `ammo_state.py` — never exit codes. FLIPPED to block: missing jsonschema lib (schema file present), state-file JSONDecodeError, hook-side missing python3/engine. LEFT fail-open: missing schema FILE (the deliberate vanished-schema fast-bail). Both engine hooks now resolve the session worktree `.venv/bin/python` before falling back to bare `python3`, so a jsonschema-less system python cannot turn every write into a block storm.
  - Writes that reach state.json through a shell variable (`F=.../state.json; jq ... > "$F"`) are now detected and validated too (path-in-variable gap closed).
- New — Sessions now hard-block `pip install` / `pip uninstall` (including `pip3`, `uv pip`, and `python -m pip` forms), so an agent can no longer corrupt the pre-provisioned session environment mid-campaign. Read-only pip commands (list, show, freeze, check) still work, and merely quoting the phrase — `grep "pip install"`, `git log --grep` — is not blocked.
  - `ammo-pip-guard.sh`: always-on PreToolUse Bash deny (exit 2 + stderr, matching the sibling-guard convention), command-position regex anchoring (handles `cd x && pip install` and env-var-prefixed forms; ignores quoted mentions), escape hatch AMMO_ALLOW_PIP=1 for the provisioning system. Harness: 25/25.
- Improved — Stage-transition guidance and state validation now come from a single state engine instead of logic duplicated across hooks, so the "next step" nudges you see after each stage are consistent, schema-aware, and match what validation will actually accept.
  - New `scripts/ammo_state.py` (~1850 lines; verbs get/set/validate/next-step/advance/enrich/backfill; identity-agnostic — reads only state.json) with a frozen `transitions.json` companion; `ammo-next-step-reminder.sh` delegates to it. Conformance suite: 535 pytest tests + all hook harnesses (11/11 suites green). Also: optional `mining_invalidated` boolean round field in the schema; status/verdict vocabulary sync-oracle test.
  - Wording aligned with the CC 2.1.198 implicit-team model everywhere the engine speaks (spawn "named champions into the implicit team", teardown via SendMessage shutdown_request/shutdown_approved drain); deflation-factor references stripped from the engine and fixtures to match the 1.12.3 schema.
- New — A saved session-babysitter workflow (`ammo-session-babysitter`) keeps an unattended campaign moving: it watches the live session, catches stalls and prompt-blocking dialogs, and nudges or recovers the session. Proven over 66 live monitoring cycles before being checked in.
- Improved — Agent instructions were de-duplicated to one canonical source per rule (shutdown protocol, nsys Stage-1 command, GATING_REQUIRED workflow, parity rules), so agents no longer receive drifting copies of the same instruction.
  - New canonical `references/shutdown-protocol.md`; per-agent shutdown blocks collapsed to a role line + pointer; SKILL.md single-owner consolidation; README regenerated; heading-based pointers across cluster-4 copies.

