### 1.12.5 (2026-06-22)
- Changed — The E2E latency sweep now times against real prompts (windowed text from the bundled GSM8K corpus) instead of uniform-random token IDs. This matters most for speculative decoding (MTP / EAGLE / ngram): on random tokens the draft and target models almost never agree, so realized acceptance collapsed to ~0 and a draft/verify kernel win was invisible in the measurement. Within a campaign baseline and opt are still measured identically (so speedup stays valid), but absolute decode_avg_s / OTPS / TPOT are no longer comparable to rounds captured before this change — re-capture your baseline if you compare across that boundary.
  - New — spec-decode rows now carry a `spec_decode` block (`draft_acceptance_rate`, `mean_acceptance_length`, raw drafts/draft_tokens/accepted counts) in `e2e_latency_results.json`, read from `llm.get_metrics()` per bucket. Purely additive: the key is absent for vanilla-decode targets, and no existing key (`avg_s`, `speedup`, the 2-stddev gate) changed.
  - Prompts are deterministic per `(input_len, output_len, batch_size)` via crc32-seeded modulo windows, so baseline and opt see identical prompts (kernel is the only A/B variable) and DP ranks build identical windows before partitioning. Legacy behavior is still reachable with `--dummy-prompt-source random`.
  - All timing runs now require the bundled `data/gsm8k_full.json` co-located with the script — there is a fail-fast startup check (skipped for `--dummy-prompt-source random`). OTPS/TPOT formula unchanged (amortized end-to-end tokens/wall-second; not physical ITL).
  - Implementation detail: applied directly to the `ai_cli_session/.claude` copy of `scripts/run_vllm_bench_latency_sweep.py` (+346 lines) — the `vllm/.claude/` copy was intentionally left untouched, so this diverges from the usual source-of-truth flow and a future `/import-ammo` would revert it unless forward-ported first. New `tests/test_sweep_real_prompts.py` (29 tests); 319 existing sweep tests still pass; adversarially reviewed + a live Qwen3-0.6B GPU smoke confirmed valid `avg_s` rows with `spec_decode` correctly absent. The `pr45717-latency-sweep.js` A/B workflow pins `--dummy-prompt-source random` (bare-file deploy, no spec-decode).

### 1.12.4 (2026-06-17)
- Updated — Sessions now build against vLLM v0.23.0 (was v0.22.1). torch (2.11.0) and the supported Python range are unchanged, but two upstream defaults flip the baseline you profile against: the Triton MoE backend is now the default on Hopper (H100/H200), and Model Runner V2 is now the default for Llama and Mistral dense models. Re-capture your baseline before comparing a fresh campaign against pre-bump numbers for those targets.
